<h2 id="h-design-philosophy-behind-the-prima-platform">Design Philosophy Behind the Prima Platform</h2>
<p>Most short-draw bows start life as a longer-draw design with smaller mods bolted on. The Prima was designed for short draw lengths from the start, so the geometry, grip and cam are matched to the archers who will actually shoot it.</p>
<p>The 30-inch axle-to-axle length keeps the bow maneuverable in blinds and treestands without feeling twitchy at full draw. At 3.93 pounds bare, it is light enough to carry all day and hold for long periods, which matters more than raw speed for many hunters. Grip shape and riser proportions are aimed at smaller hands, helping you find the same hand position shot after shot.</p>

